{"blocks":[["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/01%20Noise%20Gate/","source-block-435","Off disables the gate. The default threshold is -70 dB; the detailed setting description gives a range of -30 dB to -98 dB.",["19.8.3.1. Noise Gate"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/02%20Mic%20Detection/","source-block-335","19.8.3.2. Mic detection",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/02%20Mic%20Detection/","source-block-363","On is the default. The MicroFreak checks for a microphone whenever a vocoder preset is loaded or the Vocoder Oscillator is selected.",["19.8.3.2. Mic detection"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/02%20Mic%20Detection/","source-block-503","If no microphone is detected, the display warns “warning! mic needed”. The mic input is disabled until the next preset loads, and the vocoder filterbank is bypassed, leaving the raw Vocoder Oscillator sound.",["19.8.3.2. Mic detection"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-240","19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-282","An external audio source can modulate the vocoder, including a guitar, drum machine, phone, tablet, or Eurorack mixer. Match its output level to the MicroFreak input: these sources are usually much louder than a microphone.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-509","Approximate output levels: microphones -60 to -40 dBU; guitar -20 dBU; phones and tablets -7.78 dBU; Eurorack +13 dBU.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-631","Use a headphone/microphone splitter that connects the source to the mic contact of the MicroFreak’s 3.5 mm TRRS jack.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-754","Headphone/Microphone Splitter",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1179","CTIA/AHJ connector",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1625","Connect the device",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1650","Turn off the MicroFreak and gently remove the gooseneck microphone.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1722","Turn the external device’s output level all the way down to avoid clipping.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1804","Plug the splitter into the MicroFreak headphone jack and the device signal into the splitter’s mic branch.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1917","Turn on the MicroFreak.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1945","Set Utility > Mic Settings > Mic Detection to Off and Mic Gain initially to -12 dB.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-2041","Select a vocoder preset, hold a key, and slowly raise Mic Gain. If there is no sound, slowly raise the source device’s output level.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/Asset/01-Headphone-Microphone-Splitter/png/","source-block-57","01 Headphone Microphone Splitter",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/Asset/02-CTIA-AHJ-Connector/png/","source-block-57","02 CTIA AHJ Connector",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/","source-block-211","19.8.4. MIDI Control Center",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/","source-block-243","The MIDI Control Center for macOS and Windows can move presets between the MicroFreak and a computer and change MicroFreak settings.",["19.8.4. MIDI Control Center"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/","source-block-156","19.8.4.1. MIDI Control Center settings",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/","source-block-199","The global Vocoder settings here match those in the MicroFreak Utility menu.",["19.8.4.1. MIDI Control Center settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/","source-block-279","MIDI Control Center Vocoder settings",["19.8.4.1. MIDI Control Center settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendi